tags_func}() to support multiple\n4450 | scikit-learn versions.\n4451 | \"\"\"\n4452 | \n4453 |     for klass in type(estimator_orig).mro():\n4454 |         if (\n4455 |             # Here we check vars(...) because we want to check if the method is\n4456 |             # explicitly defined in the class instead of inherited from a parent class.\n4457 |             (\"_more_tags\" in vars(klass) or \"_get_tags\" in vars(klass))\n4458 |             and \"__sklearn_tags__\" not in vars(klass)\n4459 |         ):\n4460 |             raise TypeError(\n4461 |                 f\"Estimator {name} has defined either `_more_tags` or `_get_tags`,\"\n4462 |                 \" but not `__sklearn_tags__`. If you're customizing tags, and need to\"\n4463 |                 \" support multiple scikit-learn versions, you can implement both\"\n4464 |                 \" `__sklearn_tags__` and `_more_tags` or `_get_tags`. This change was\"\n4465 |                 \" introduced in scikit-learn=1.6\"\n4466 |             )\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"_get_tags\", \"_more_tags\", \"safe_tags\", \"_get_tags _more_tags safe_tags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/validation.py:validate_data`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2824 | def validate_data(\n2825 |     _estimator,\n2826 |     /,\n2827 |     X=\"no_validation\",\n2828 |     y=\"no_validation\",\n2829 |     reset=True,\n2830 |     validate_separately=False,\n2831 |     skip_check_array=False,\n2832 |     **check_params,\n2833 | ):\n2834 |     \"\"\"Validate input data and set or check feature names and counts of the input.\n2835 | \n2836 |     This helper function should be used in an estimator that requires input\n2837 |     validation. This mutates the estimator and sets the `n_features_in_` and\n2838 |     `feature_names_in_` attributes if `reset=True`.\n2839 | \n2840 |     .. versionadded:: 1.6\n2841 | \n2842 |     Parameters\n2843 |     ----------\n2844 |     _estimator :