e ``=``\n58 |     as a substitute for ``==``.\n59 | \n60 |     Parameters\n61 |     ----------\n62 |     tok : tuple of int, str\n63 |         ints correspond to the all caps constants in the tokenize module\n64 | \n65 |     Returns\n66 |     -------\n67 |     tuple of int, str\n68 |         Either the input or token or the replacement values\n69 |     \"\"\"\n70 |     toknum, tokval = tok\n71 |     return toknum, \"==\" if tokval == \"=\" else tokval\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/io/pytables.py:Fixed.version`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2789 | def version(self) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n2790 |         \"\"\"compute and set our version\"\"\"\n2791 |         version = getattr(self.group._v_attrs, \"pandas_version\", None)\n2792 |         if isinstance(version, str):\n2793 |             version_tup = tuple(int(x) for x in version.split(\".\"))\n2794 |             if len(version_tup) == 2:\n2795 |                 version_tup = version_tup + (0,)\n2796 |             assert len(version_tup) == 3  # needed for mypy\n2797 |             return version_tup\n2798 |         else:\n2799 |             return (0, 0, 0)\n```\n\nFound file `pandas/core/computation/pytables.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `pandas/core/computation/pytables.py` for the full content if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Let me look specifically at the `_validate_where` function since it's mentioned in the issue:\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['pandas/core/computation/pytables.py:_validate_where']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `pandas/core/computation/pytables.py:_validate_where`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/computation/pytables.py:_validate_where`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `pandas/core/co