e : Returns a Styler object for applying CSS-like styles.\n603 |     io.formats.style.Styler : Helps style a DataFrame or Series according to the\n604 |         data with HTML and CSS.\n605 |     io.formats.style.Styler.to_excel : Export styled DataFrame to Excel.\n606 |     io.formats.style.Styler.to_html : Export styled DataFrame to HTML.\n607 | \n608 |     Examples\n609 |     --------\n610 |     >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"A\": [1, 1, 1]})\n611 |     >>> df.style.map(lambda x: \"background-color: blueGreenRed;\").to_excel(\n612 |     ...     \"styled.xlsx\"\n613 |     ... )  # doctest: +SKIP\n614 |     CSSWarning: Unhandled color format: 'blueGreenRed'\n615 |     >>> df.style.map(lambda x: \"border: 1px solid red red;\").to_excel(\n616 |     ...     \"styled.xlsx\"\n617 |     ... )  # doctest: +SKIP\n618 |     CSSWarning: Unhandled color format: 'blueGreenRed'\n619 |     \"\"\"\n```\n\nFound file `pandas/core/interchange/dataframe.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `pandas/core/interchange/dataframe.py` for the full content if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Let me search for the specific implementation of the `merge_cells` parameter in the Excel formatting code:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['ExcelFormatter', 'merge_cells']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\npandas/io/formats/excel.py:ExcelFormatter.__init__\npandas/io/formats/style.py:Styler.to_excel\npandas/io/formats/excel.py:ExcelFormatter._format_hierarchical_rows\npandas/io/formats/excel.py:ExcelFormatter._format_header_mi\npandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame.to_excel\npandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame.to_json\npandas/io/formats/excel.py:ExcelFormatter\npandas/io/excel/_openpyxl.py:OpenpyxlWriter._write_cells\npandas/core/computation/pytables.py:TermValue\npandas/core/computation/pytables.py:TermValue.__init